Create a `SnackBar` with the message you want and use the `ScaffoldMessenger` to display it. For example, inside a button’s `onPressed` you can write:
```dart
final snackBar = SnackBar(content: const Text('Action completed'));
ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(snackBar);
```
This shows a brief message at the bottom of the screen after the action completes.

First add the font files to your project and declare them in the `pubspec.yaml` under a `fonts` block, giving each a `family` name (e.g., Raleway). Then set that family as the default by assigning its name to the `fontFamily` property of the app's `ThemeData` in `MaterialApp`. Example:
```dart
return MaterialApp(
  title: 'Custom Fonts',
  theme: ThemeData(fontFamily: 'Raleway'),
  home: const MyHomePage(),
);
```

Put the business logic in a ViewModel class that lives in its own layer between the UI screens and the data model, and have that class extend `ChangeNotifier`. Inside the ViewModel expose the state you need (e.g., loading flags, data objects) and call `notifyListeners()` whenever you modify it. Provide the same ViewModel instance to each screen (for example with the `provider` package) so all screens listen to the same notifier and share the state. A minimal example is:
```dart
class CartModel extends ChangeNotifier {
  final List<Item> _items = [];
  UnmodifiableListView<Item> get items => UnmodifiableListView(_items);
  void add(Item item) {
    _items.add(item);
    notifyListeners();
  }
}
```

Binlerce öğeyi verimli bir şekilde göstermek için `ListView.builder` kullanın; bu yapı, yalnızca ekranda görünen öğeleri oluşturur ve geri kalanları geri dönüşümle yönetir. `itemCount` ile öğe sayısını, `itemBuilder` ile her bir öğeyi bir widget (ör. `ListTile`) olarak döndürün. Gerekirse `prototypeItem` ile öğe yüksekliğini önceden tanımlayabilirsiniz. ```dart
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: items.length,
  prototypeItem: ListTile(title: Text(items.first)),
  itemBuilder: (context, index) {
    return ListTile(title: Text(items[index]));
  },
)
```
